filsys 1.0.0 (2026-08-27)
========================

First stable release: V4, V5, V6, V7 and 32V filesystems, read-write and
read-only, feature complete and tested against real images.

- Mount V4/V5/V6 (identical on disk), V7 (PDP-11) and 32V (VAX) images.
- Middle-endian (PDP-11) and little-endian (VAX) byte-order handling, including
  the VAX 4-byte-aligned superblock field offsets.
- Read/write/mkdir/rmdir/unlink/rename/chmod/chown/truncate/utimens/statfs.
- Free-list and inode-table integrity check with -c.
- Partition mounting with -o offset=, and nested mounts of two partitions of
  one disk.
- filsysfind: locate filesystem superblocks (partitions) on a raw image.
- No lock on the image, so several partitions of one disk can be mounted at
  once.
